      "body": "## Motivation\n\nSince #46988, `allocation._storage()` reads `tree_cache.req_to_token_pool`. The `TreeCacheNamespace` dummy cache that `bench_one_batch`'s `extend()` builds doesn't set that attribute, so `batch.prepare_for_extend()` fails:\n\n```\nsglang/srt/mem_cache/allocation.py:160, in _storage\n    tree_cache.req_to_token_pool,\nAttributeError: 'TreeCacheNamespace' object has no attribute 'req_to_token_pool'\n```\n\nThis is currently failing XPU stage-a on every PR that reaches it (`test/registered/xpu/test_breakable_cuda_graph.py`, `test/registered/xpu/test_intel_xpu_backend.py`), e.g. job 123227153721. CI Retry doesn't retry it because the error is an AttributeError.\n\n## Modifications\n\nPass `req_to_token_pool=model_runner.req_to_token_pool` to the dummy tree cache. Its other `tree_cache` reads (`rotation_base_of`, SWA retain) only run with a cached prefix or SWA, and this benchmark uses neither.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `py_compile` and `pre-commit run` on the changed file pass.\n- XPU stage-a in this PR's CI checks the fix end to end.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #40813401206](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40813401206)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40813401194](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40813401194)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #40813401208](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40813401208)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
